AltTab Free-tier patch
======================

Removes the 14-day Pro trial and every upgrade prompt from AltTab, leaving the permanent
Free tier, with one deliberate exception: the second shortcut slot works. It is AltTab's own
default (hold ⌥ and press the key above Tab to switch between the active app's windows),
which the official Free tier blocks at the key press. Every other Pro feature stays locked:
App Icons and Titles styles, Auto size, Search, Search-on-release, shortcut slots 3-9.

Base: lwouis/alt-tab-macos tag v11.7.1 (https://github.com/lwouis/alt-tab-macos)
Apply: git apply free.patch            (from the repo root)
Build + install: ~/.config/alttab/bin/alttab-free-build

What it changes
  LicenseManager        state is always .trialExpired; no trialStartDate written, no Keychain
                        read, no license-server call
  ProTransitionManager  Day 1/4/12/15/21/35 windows, popovers and badge are never emitted;
                        the timed scheduler is never armed; no free pass for gated features;
                        hard-gated features are refused, except shortcut slot 2
  ControlsTab           the "+" button may re-add slot 2; slots 3-9 stay locked
  Menubar               no "Get Pro" / "My Account" items ("Support this project" stays)
  SettingsWindow        no Upgrade button in the sidebar
  UpgradeTab            Pro-only controls snap back silently instead of opening the Upgrade page
  App                   first-launch Settings no longer waits for the Welcome letter

